-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 1א', §1.10 ליווי תלמידים
-- Accompanying pupils: pay for out-of-school activity in activity units,
-- the extra pay for a rest day, principals, reporting and payment; pay for
-- sea voyages; per diem; and the personal-accident cover for teachers on
-- trips (§1.10.1).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `1.10 ליווי תלמידים`

-- The actors of the insurance cover, which the takanon's shared Party list lacks.
@desc Actors of section 1.10.1 (the accident cover) that are not in the takanon's shared Party list.
DECLARE `1.10 party` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer`
    `the insured or his representative`
    `the exceptional-cases committee`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10/p2 The page's table of contents (heading).
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10/p4 Entries of the table of contents, naming the two subsections encoded below.

§§ `1.10.0.1 ליווי תלמידים בטיולים ובפעילות חוץ בית ספרית`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p1 A heading: "1. ליווי תלמידים בטיולים ובפעילות חוץ בית ספרית".

@desc One outing with pupils outside the educational institution, as section 1.10.0 asks about it.
DECLARE `outing` HAS
    `starts in the morning`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `start hour`                IS A NUMBER  @desc 24-hour clock
    `end hour`                  IS A NUMBER  @desc 24-hour clock on the day it starts; past midnight is above 24 (1:00 the next day is 25)
    `nights`                    IS A NUMBER  @desc nights of lodging the outing includes
    `end hour of the last day`  IS A NUMBER  @desc for an outing with lodging, the hour it ends on its last day

DECLARE `activity kind` IS ONE OF
    `ending between 14:00 and 15:00`
    `ending between 15:00 and 18:00`
    `ending between 18:00 and 21:00`
    `ending between 21:00 and 24:00`
    `detached, between 16:00 and 24:00`
    `with lodging`

-- א AS PRINTED: an outing is out-of-school activity if it is one of six
-- kinds, each read with its bounds inclusive, so the table can be asked
-- directly.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p4 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p5 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p6 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p7 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p8
GIVEN o IS AN `outing`
GIVETH A LIST OF `activity kind`
DECIDE `the kinds the outing fits as printed` o IS
    filter (GIVEN k YIELD
                CONSIDER k
                WHEN `ending between 14:00 and 15:00` THEN o's `nights` EQUALS 0 AND o's `starts in the morning` AND o's `end hour` AT LEAST 14 AND o's `end hour` AT MOST 15
                WHEN `ending between 15:00 and 18:00` THEN o's `nights` EQUALS 0 AND o's `starts in the morning` AND o's `end hour` AT LEAST 15 AND o's `end hour` AT MOST 18
                WHEN `ending between 18:00 and 21:00` THEN o's `nights` EQUALS 0 AND o's `starts in the morning` AND o's `end hour` AT LEAST 18 AND o's `end hour` AT MOST 21
                WHEN `ending between 21:00 and 24:00` THEN o's `nights` EQUALS 0 AND o's `starts in the morning` AND o's `end hour` AT LEAST 21 AND o's `end hour` AT MOST 24
                WHEN `detached, between 16:00 and 24:00` THEN o's `nights` EQUALS 0 AND (NOT o's `starts in the morning`) AND o's `start hour` AT LEAST 16 AND o's `end hour` AT MOST 24
                WHEN `with lodging` THEN o's `nights` AT LEAST 1 AND o's `starts in the morning`)
           (LIST `ending between 14:00 and 15:00`, `ending between 15:00 and 18:00`,
                 `ending between 18:00 and 21:00`, `ending between 21:00 and 24:00`,
                 `detached, between 16:00 and 24:00`, `with lodging`)

-- ג's units, row by row.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p11 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p12 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p13 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p14 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p15 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p16 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p17 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p18 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p19 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p20 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p21 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p22 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p23
GIVEN k IS AN `activity kind`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `units for` k IS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `ending between 14:00 and 15:00` THEN 0.5
    WHEN `ending between 15:00 and 18:00` THEN 2
    WHEN `ending between 18:00 and 21:00` THEN 3.5
    WHEN `ending between 21:00 and 24:00` THEN 5
    WHEN `detached, between 16:00 and 24:00` THEN 3
    WHEN `with lodging` THEN 7

-- F-1.10-a: an outing from the morning that ends at 15:00, 18:00 or 21:00
-- fits two rows. The reading adopted: the row that OPENS at that hour
-- governs it, as F-1.7-a reads the same shape of table.
-- F-1.10-b: "one (only) of these" leaves out an outing that starts after
-- the morning but before 16:00, and one from the morning that ends after
-- midnight without lodging; read by the letter, neither earns units.
GIVEN `starts in the morning` IS A BOOLEAN, `start hour` IS A NUMBER, `end hour` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `units for a day without lodging` `starts in the morning` `start hour` `end hour` IS
    IF `starts in the morning`
    THEN BRANCH IF `end hour` GREATER THAN 24 THEN 0
                IF `end hour` AT LEAST 21 THEN 5
                IF `end hour` AT LEAST 18 THEN 3.5
                IF `end hour` AT LEAST 15 THEN 2
                IF `end hour` AT LEAST 14 THEN 0.5
                OTHERWISE 0
    ELSE IF `start hour` AT LEAST 16 AND `end hour` AT MOST 24 THEN 3 ELSE 0

-- ד: only the units of the row of the outing's end; never added up for one
-- outing, but by nights where there is more than one night; and the last
-- day, without lodging, by its end hour. F-1.10-d: whether that last-day
-- sentence reaches a ONE-night outing, which row 6 already describes as
-- ending the next day, is not said; the reading adopted applies it to every
-- outing with lodging, as its words name no number of nights.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p24
GIVEN o IS AN `outing`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `activity units` o IS
    IF o's `nights` AT LEAST 1
    THEN `units for` `with lodging` TIMES o's `nights`
             PLUS `units for a day without lodging` TRUE 8 (o's `end hour of the last day`)
    ELSE `units for a day without lodging` (o's `starts in the morning`) (o's `start hour`) (o's `end hour`)

`an outing ending at 15:00 fits two rows` MEANS
    count (`the kinds the outing fits as printed` (`outing` WITH
        `starts in the morning` IS TRUE, `start hour` IS 8, `end hour` IS 15, `nights` IS 0, `end hour of the last day` IS 15))
    EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `an outing ending at 15:00 fits two rows`

`an outing from 15:00 to 20:00 fits no row` MEANS
    null (`the kinds the outing fits as printed` (`outing` WITH
        `starts in the morning` IS FALSE, `start hour` IS 15, `end hour` IS 20, `nights` IS 0, `end hour of the last day` IS 20))
`an outing from the morning to 1:00 fits no row` MEANS
    null (`the kinds the outing fits as printed` (`outing` WITH
        `starts in the morning` IS TRUE, `start hour` IS 8, `end hour` IS 25, `nights` IS 0, `end hour of the last day` IS 25))
#ASSERT `an outing from 15:00 to 20:00 fits no row` AND `an outing from the morning to 1:00 fits no row`

-- F-1.10-d's evidence: one night, home at 17:00 the next day.
`one night, home at 17:00` MEANS
    `outing` WITH `starts in the morning` IS TRUE, `start hour` IS 8, `end hour` IS 17, `nights` IS 1, `end hour of the last day` IS 17
`the last-day sentence changes the units of a one-night outing` MEANS
    (NOT (`activity units` `one night, home at 17:00` EQUALS `units for` `with lodging`))
#ASSERT `the last-day sentence changes the units of a one-night outing`

-- ב: one unit is 0.7% of the monthly combined salary with the 3% (2001),
-- 2008 and 2011 supplements, by the position and up to one position.
@desc The salary components a base is made of.
DECLARE `base component` IS ONE OF
    `combined salary`, `3% supplement`, `2008 supplement`, `2011 supplement`, `1994 teaching supplement`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p9 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p10
`the components of a unit as section 1.10.0 lists them` MEANS
    LIST `combined salary`, `3% supplement`, `2008 supplement`, `2011 supplement`

GIVEN `full-position base` IS A NUMBER, `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `value of an activity unit` `full-position base` `position fraction` IS
    0.7% TIMES `full-position base` TIMES min `position fraction` 1

-- F-1.10-c: section 1.1ו lists this allowance (ו.3) among the percentage
-- allowances it computes on the combined salary with the 3%, 2008, 2011
-- AND 1994 supplements. Quoted here for the evidence only; the reading
-- adopted is section 1.10.0's own list, the particular one.
`the components section 1.1ו gives the percentage allowances` MEANS
    LIST `combined salary`, `3% supplement`, `2008 supplement`, `2011 supplement`, `1994 teaching supplement`
`sections 1.10.0 and 1.1ו give the activity unit different bases` MEANS
    (NOT (`the components of a unit as section 1.10.0 lists them` EQUALS `the components section 1.1ו gives the percentage allowances`))
#ASSERT `sections 1.10.0 and 1.1ו give the activity unit different bases`

DECLARE `outing action` IS ONE OF
    `pay for the outing` HAS `outing pay` IS A NUMBER
    `submit the list of accompanying teachers`

-- ה: paid with the salary for the month after the activity. Time in
-- salary months from the activity's month: 1 is the next month's salary.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p25
GIVEN `pay owed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `outing action`
DECIDE `payment with the next month's salary` `pay owed` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay for the outing` paid PROVIDED paid AT LEAST `pay owed`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 1.10.0: paid with the salary for the month after the activity"

DECLARE `salary use` IS ONE OF
    `hour value`, `pension`, `further-training fund`, `provident fund`, `severance pay`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p26
GIVEN u IS A `salary use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `activity pay counts as salary for` u IF
    FALSE

-- ז: the earlier arrangements are cancelled, but the sums paid before for
-- lodging and for activity ending after 16:00 are still paid, subject to
-- the collective agreements. F-1.10-e: whether in ADDITION to the units or
-- INSTEAD of them is not said; the reading adopted is in addition.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p27 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p28
GIVEN o IS AN `outing`, `sum paid before for such outings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `earlier sum still paid` o `sum paid before for such outings` IS
    IF o's `nights` AT LEAST 1 OR o's `end hour` GREATER THAN 16
    THEN `sum paid before for such outings`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN o IS AN `outing`, `sum paid before for such outings` IS A NUMBER, `unit value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `outing pay instead of the earlier sum` o `sum paid before for such outings` `unit value` IS
    IF `earlier sum still paid` o `sum paid before for such outings` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `sum paid before for such outings`
    ELSE `activity units` o TIMES `unit value`

-- ח: not for של"ח teachers, whose earlier arrangement stays (section 6.17).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p29
GIVEN `is a של"ח teacher` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unit arrangement applies` `is a של"ח teacher` IF
    (NOT `is a של"ח teacher`)

@export default The pay for one outing with pupils under section 1.10.0 of the takanon: its activity units at the unit value, with the earlier sums still paid
GIVEN o IS AN `outing` @desc the outing
      `full-position base` IS A NUMBER @desc the monthly combined salary for one full position with the 3%, 2008 and 2011 supplements
      `position fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a full position held
      `sum paid before for such outings` IS A NUMBER @desc what the arrangements before this one paid for such an outing; 0 if none
      `is a של"ח teacher` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `outing pay` o `full-position base` `position fraction` `sum paid before for such outings` `is a של"ח teacher` IS
    IF `the unit arrangement applies` `is a של"ח teacher`
    THEN `activity units` o TIMES `value of an activity unit` `full-position base` `position fraction`
             PLUS `earlier sum still paid` o `sum paid before for such outings`
    ELSE 0

-- ט: on a rest day or a day he does not teach, 4 hours more; on a day of
-- some teaching, the table. F-1.10-f: its first row (1 hour taught → 1 hour
-- paid) breaks the pattern of the others, under which every row and the
-- day without teaching come to 4 hours in all; the printed value is kept.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p30 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p31 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p32 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p33 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p34 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p35 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p36 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p37 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p38 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p39
GIVEN `hours taught that day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `extra hours for accompanying on a rest or non-teaching day` `hours taught that day` IS
    BRANCH IF `hours taught that day` AT LEAST 4 THEN 0
           IF `hours taught that day` EQUALS 3 THEN 1
           IF `hours taught that day` EQUALS 2 THEN 2
           IF `hours taught that day` EQUALS 1 THEN 1
           OTHERWISE 4

`the first row of the partial-day table breaks the four-hour pattern` MEANS
        all (GIVEN h YIELD h PLUS `extra hours for accompanying on a rest or non-teaching day` h EQUALS 4) (LIST 0, 2, 3)
    AND (NOT (1 PLUS `extra hours for accompanying on a rest or non-teaching day` 1 EQUALS 4))
#ASSERT `the first row of the partial-day table breaks the four-hour pattern`

-- י: a principal is paid as an accompanying teacher if he coordinates the
-- trip, or if he educates the class he accompanies; one who only
-- accompanies is not. F-1.10-g: a principal who educates the class and does
-- not coordinate meets ¶41 (paid) and ¶42 (not paid); the reading adopted
-- is ¶41, the particular case.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p40 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p41 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p42
GIVEN `coordinates the trip` IS A BOOLEAN, `educates the class he accompanies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a principal is paid for the trip` `coordinates the trip` `educates the class he accompanies` IF
    `coordinates the trip` OR `educates the class he accompanies`

-- ¶42 as printed: one who accompanies and does not coordinate is not paid.
GIVEN `coordinates the trip` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a principal is paid under ¶42 as printed` `coordinates the trip` IF
    `coordinates the trip`

`¶41 and ¶42 part on a class-educating principal who does not coordinate` MEANS
        `a principal is paid for the trip` FALSE TRUE
    AND (NOT `a principal is paid under ¶42 as printed` FALSE)
#ASSERT `¶41 and ¶42 part on a class-educating principal who does not coordinate`

-- יא: trips to Poland on the same terms.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p43
GIVEN `trip to Poland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the same allowance and criteria apply` `trip to Poland` IF
    TRUE

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p44 A heading: "הוראת ביצוע".

-- The principals report at the end of each period of trips: name, identity
-- number, dates, and end hour or kind of activity.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p45 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p46 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p47 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p48 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p49 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p50
DECLARE `report line` HAS
    `teacher's name`               IS A STRING
    `identity number`              IS A STRING
    `dates accompanied`            IS A LIST OF DATE
    `end hour or kind of activity` IS A STRING

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `outing action`
DECIDE `the principal reports the accompanying teachers` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `submit the list of accompanying teachers`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.10.0: at the end of each trip period the principal sends the list of accompanying teachers"

DECLARE `employment` IS ONE OF `a state employee`, `not a state employee`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p51 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p52
GIVEN e IS AN `employment`
GIVETH A Party
DECIDE `who pays for accompanying` e IS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `a state employee` THEN `the Ministry of Education`
    WHEN `not a state employee` THEN `the local authority or owning body`

§§ `1.10.0.2 ליווי תלמידים בהפלגות בים`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p53 A heading: "2. ליווי תלמידים מבתי-ספר על-יסודיים בהפלגות בים".
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p54 A heading: "א. הגדרות".

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p55 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p59
GIVEN `a day of the study period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a day of vacation, Sabbath or holiday` `a day of the study period` IF
    (NOT `a day of the study period`)

-- "A voyage day" is a whole day or part of one: 80 hours is four days.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p56
GIVEN hours IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `voyage days` hours IS
    CEILING (hours DIVIDED BY 24)

#ASSERT `voyage days` 80 EQUALS 4

-- "Salary of one position": the combined salary for one full position by
-- grade and recognised seniority; the day's salary is a 26th of it.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p57 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p58
GIVEN `combined salary of one full position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a sea teacher's salary for a voyage day` `combined salary of one full position` IS
    `combined salary of one full position` DIVIDED BY 26

DECLARE `craft` IS ONE OF `a boat`, `a ship`, `a navy vessel`, `a large vessel`
DECLARE `place aboard` IS ONE OF `sole or lead accompanier`, `second or further accompanier`

@desc One voyage of a sea teacher or sea instructor with pupils.
DECLARE `voyage` HAS
    `craft sailed`                IS A `craft`
    `place`                       IS A `place aboard`
    `accompaniers aboard`         IS A NUMBER
    `voyage days in study period` IS A NUMBER
    `voyage days in vacation, Sabbaths and holidays` IS A NUMBER
    `in charge of 3 craft or more` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a class educator`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `voyage days already sailed this year` IS A NUMBER

-- ב: the rates, in percent of the day's salary, on top of the regular
-- salary. (3)–(4): a navy vessel is a ship. F-1.10-h: row (1) is the sole
-- accompanier, or the lead one "in a boat with two accompaniers"; the lead
-- of a boat with three or more has no row. The reading adopted: row (1).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p60 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p61 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p62 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p63 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p64 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p65 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p66 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p67 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p68 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p69 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p70 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p71 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p72 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p73 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p74 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p75 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p76 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p77 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p78 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p79 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p80
GIVEN c IS A `craft`, p IS A `place aboard`, `in the study period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `voyage rate` c p `in the study period` IS
    `row` PLUS (IF `in the study period` THEN 0 ELSE 100)
    WHERE
        `row` MEANS
            CONSIDER c
            WHEN `a boat` THEN IF p EQUALS `sole or lead accompanier` THEN 160 ELSE 100
            WHEN `a large vessel` THEN IF p EQUALS `sole or lead accompanier` THEN 60 ELSE 40
            OTHERWISE IF p EQUALS `sole or lead accompanier` THEN 100 ELSE 80

-- The lead of a boat as row (1) prints it: "with two accompaniers".
GIVEN v IS A `voyage`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `row (1) as printed takes the lead of this boat` v IF
        v's `craft sailed` EQUALS `a boat`
    AND v's `place` EQUALS `sole or lead accompanier`
    AND (v's `accompaniers aboard` EQUALS 1 OR v's `accompaniers aboard` EQUALS 2)

-- ג: in charge of 3 craft or more, 10% more. ד: a sea teacher who is a class
-- educator sails 3 voyage days a year for no extra pay.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p81 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p82
GIVEN v IS A `voyage`, `day's salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `voyage pay` v `day's salary` IS
    (`day's salary` DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES
        (  `voyage rate` (v's `craft sailed`) (v's `place`) TRUE  TIMES `paid study days`
         + `voyage rate` (v's `craft sailed`) (v's `place`) FALSE TIMES v's `voyage days in vacation, Sabbaths and holidays`
         + (IF v's `in charge of 3 craft or more` THEN 10 ELSE 0)
               TIMES (`paid study days` PLUS v's `voyage days in vacation, Sabbaths and holidays`))
    WHERE
        `unpaid days left` MEANS
            IF v's `is a class educator`
            THEN max 0 (3 MINUS v's `voyage days already sailed this year`)
            ELSE 0
        `paid study days` MEANS
            max 0 (v's `voyage days in study period` MINUS `unpaid days left`)

§§ `1.10.0.3 אש"ל למורים`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p83 A heading: "3. אש\"ל למורים".

DECLARE `accompanied setting` IS ONE OF
    `trips and journeys, including Gadna`
    `national service`
    `an army training base`
    `a trip where the employer provides lodging and food`

-- א–ב and the note: food money as for civil servants (takshir 26.231, the
-- meals by 26.222 and 26.232), not where meals are had in the kibbutz or
-- base, or provided by the employer. The takshir amount is an input.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p84 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p85 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p86
GIVEN s IS AN `accompanied setting`, `food money by the takshir` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `food money` s `food money by the takshir` IS
    IF s EQUALS `trips and journeys, including Gadna`
    THEN `food money by the takshir`
    ELSE 0

-- ג: Mediterranean voyages: 20% of the destination's daily rate per day at
-- sea, 60% of the country's rate per day ashore, by the takshir; hotel and
-- like costs paid by the school are set off; the supervisor states that sea
-- days and port days run one to one. In force from 1.3.84.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p87 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p88 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p89 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p90 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p92
GIVEN `days at sea` IS A NUMBER
      `days ashore` IS A NUMBER
      `daily rate of the destination` IS A NUMBER
      `daily rate of the country ashore` IS A NUMBER
      `costs the school paid in full` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Mediterranean per diem` `days at sea` `days ashore` `daily rate of the destination` `daily rate of the country ashore` `costs the school paid in full` IS
    max 0 (20% TIMES `daily rate of the destination` TIMES `days at sea`
           PLUS 60% TIMES `daily rate of the country ashore` TIMES `days ashore`
           MINUS `costs the school paid in full`)

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p91
GIVEN `days of a Mediterranean voyage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days at sea of a Mediterranean voyage` `days of a Mediterranean voyage` IS
    `days of a Mediterranean voyage` DIVIDED BY 2

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p93 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p94 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p95 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p96 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p97 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p98 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p99 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p100 The subsection's sources (אסמכתא), 1–7.
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p101 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p102 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p103 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p104 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p105 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p106 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_0/p107 The subsection's sources (אסמכתא), 8–14.

§§ `1.10.1 ביטוח עובדי הוראה המשתתפים במסעות וטיולים`

@desc An accident to a covered teaching employee on a trip, as section 1.10.1 asks about it.
DECLARE `trip accident` HAS
    `covered by the Ministry's instructions`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `on a trip, tour or journey in the course of school work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `between leaving home and coming straight back` IS A BOOLEAN
    `covered by the road-accident or hostile-action laws` IS A BOOLEAN
    `excluded cause`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc self-harm or suicide, needless danger, an offence other than a traffic offence, insanity, drunkenness or drugs (1.10.1.3)
    `insured by another insurer`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `died of it within 12 months`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `disability percent`                        IS A NUMBER @desc permanent disability, 0–100
    `weeks unfit for work`                      IS A NUMBER
    `national-insurance payments stopped at 26 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months unfit within the first 26 weeks`    IS A NUMBER
    `notice reached the insurer within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 1א–ב, ו–ז: who is covered and when; death or 100% permanent disability
-- pays 30,000 dollars in shekels once, partial disability its share.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_a akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_f akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_g
GIVEN a IS A `trip accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cover applies` a IF
        a's `covered by the Ministry's instructions`
    AND a's `on a trip, tour or journey in the course of school work`
    AND a's `between leaving home and coming straight back`
    AND (NOT a's `covered by the road-accident or hostile-action laws`)
    AND (NOT a's `excluded cause`)
    AND a's `notice reached the insurer within 6 months`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_a/p2 A note: the amounts are those of the 1997 cover terms, in force since.

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_b
`the sum for death or full disability, in dollars` MEANS 30000

-- 1ג: weekly 450 dollars from week 27 to the end of a year from the injury,
-- where national-insurance payments stopped only by their 26-week limit.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_c
GIVEN a IS A `trip accident`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weekly compensation in dollars` a IS
    IF `the cover applies` a AND a's `national-insurance payments stopped at 26 weeks`
    THEN 450 TIMES max 0 (min (a's `weeks unfit for work`) 52 MINUS 26)
    ELSE 0

-- 1ד: unfit at least two weeks in a row: 200 dollars a month while unfit,
-- up to week 26.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_d
GIVEN a IS A `trip accident`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `monthly expenses in dollars` a IS
    IF `the cover applies` a AND a's `weeks unfit for work` AT LEAST 2
    THEN 200 TIMES a's `months unfit within the first 26 weeks`
    ELSE 0

-- 1ה: the committee may, by majority, on a representative organisation's
-- request, pay from 10 days after the injury; raise the weekly sum or pay
-- it longer, by no more than 10% of what the injured is owed; and
-- recommend up to 450 dollars for the family's travel to a far accident.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_e akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_e/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_e/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_e/p4
GIVEN `owed` IS A NUMBER, `increase the committee decides` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `committee increase allowed` `owed` `increase the committee decides` IS
    min `increase the committee decides` (10% TIMES `owed`)

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_e/p5 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_e/p6
GIVEN `family's travel costs in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `special compensation for a far accident` `family's travel costs in dollars` IS
    min `family's travel costs in dollars` 450

DECLARE `cover action` IS ONE OF
    `report the accident to Inbal`
    `notify the insurer in writing`
    `send the accident report and doctor's certificate`
    `cooperate with the insurer`
    `decide on an exceptional case`

-- 1א (the accident report): the principal reports within two weeks (time
-- in days).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_g/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_g/p3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `cover action`
DECIDE `the principal reports the accident` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `report the accident to Inbal`
    WITHIN 14
    LEST BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.10.1: a teacher hurt on a trip is reported within two weeks"

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_1__subpara_g/p4 The line introducing the sample report form; the form is not a rule.

-- 2א–ג: the insurer pays the table's percent of the insured sum for an
-- immediate disability within 12 months of the accident, or the sum on
-- death within 12 months.
DECLARE `listed injury` IS ONE OF
    `complete paralysis`, `loss of two limbs`, `loss of both hands or all fingers and both thumbs`,
    `permanent confinement to bed`, `any other total loss of working capacity`, `total loss of sight of both eyes`,
    `loss of the arm at the shoulder`, `between shoulder and elbow`, `at the elbow`, `between elbow and wrist`,
    `loss of the hand`, `loss of four fingers and thumb of one hand`, `loss of four fingers`,
    `thumb, two bones`, `thumb, one bone`,
    `index finger, three bones`, `index finger, two bones`, `index finger, one bone`,
    `middle finger, three bones`, `middle finger, two bones`, `middle finger, one bone`,
    `ring finger, three bones`, `ring finger, two bones`, `ring finger, one bone`,
    `little finger, three bones`, `little finger, two bones`, `little finger, one bone`,
    `loss of the leg at the thigh`, `between knee and thigh`, `below the knee`,
    `all the toes`, `big toe, two bones`, `big toe, one bone`, `another toe, where more than one is lost`,
    `a whole eye`, `sight, apart from light perception`, `the lens of the eye`,
    `hearing of both ears`, `hearing of one ear`

-- "אבדן ארבע אצבעות אבדן הבוהן: 35%" is read as two lines run together:
-- four fingers at 35%, and the thumb's two rows (25%, 10%) under it.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p4 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p5 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p6 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p7 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p8 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p9 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p10 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p11 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p12 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p13 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p14 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p15 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p16 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p17 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p18 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p19 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p20
GIVEN i IS A `listed injury`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `percent in the table` i IS
    CONSIDER i
    WHEN `loss of the arm at the shoulder` THEN 60
    WHEN `between shoulder and elbow` THEN 50
    WHEN `at the elbow` THEN 47.5
    WHEN `between elbow and wrist` THEN 45
    WHEN `loss of the hand` THEN 42.5
    WHEN `loss of four fingers and thumb of one hand` THEN 42.5
    WHEN `loss of four fingers` THEN 35
    WHEN `thumb, two bones` THEN 25
    WHEN `thumb, one bone` THEN 10
    WHEN `index finger, three bones` THEN 10
    WHEN `index finger, two bones` THEN 8
    WHEN `index finger, one bone` THEN 4
    WHEN `middle finger, three bones` THEN 6
    WHEN `middle finger, two bones` THEN 4
    WHEN `middle finger, one bone` THEN 2
    WHEN `ring finger, three bones` THEN 5
    WHEN `ring finger, two bones` THEN 4
    WHEN `ring finger, one bone` THEN 2
    WHEN `little finger, three bones` THEN 4
    WHEN `little finger, two bones` THEN 3
    WHEN `little finger, one bone` THEN 2
    WHEN `loss of the leg at the thigh` THEN 70
    WHEN `between knee and thigh` THEN 50
    WHEN `below the knee` THEN 35
    WHEN `all the toes` THEN 15
    WHEN `big toe, two bones` THEN 5
    WHEN `big toe, one bone` THEN 2
    WHEN `another toe, where more than one is lost` THEN 1
    WHEN `a whole eye` THEN 30
    WHEN `sight, apart from light perception` THEN 30
    WHEN `the lens of the eye` THEN 20
    WHEN `hearing of both ears` THEN 50
    WHEN `hearing of one ear` THEN 7
    OTHERWISE 100

-- The rest of the table's rows (¶21–40) are encoded in the function above.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p21 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p22 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p23 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p24 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p25 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p26 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p27 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p28 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p29 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p30 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p31 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p32 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p33 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p34 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p35 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p36 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p37 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p38 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p39 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_c/p40
`the table's rows are read` MEANS
    `percent in the table` `hearing of one ear` EQUALS 7 AND `percent in the table` `complete paralysis` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the table's rows are read`


-- 2ד: an injury not in the table, or the table not usable, by the
-- national-insurance regulations, through a doctor at the insurer's cost.
-- F-1.10-i: 1ב sends EVERY partial disability to those regulations, so a
-- listed injury has two measures. The reading adopted: the table for a
-- listed injury (2ג–ד, the cover's own terms), the regulations otherwise.
DECLARE `measure of disability` IS ONE OF `the cover's table`, `the national-insurance regulations`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_d
GIVEN `the injury is listed and the table usable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `measure of disability`
DECIDE `the measure under 2ד` `the injury is listed and the table usable` IS
    IF `the injury is listed and the table usable`
    THEN `the cover's table`
    ELSE `the national-insurance regulations`

GIVEN `the injury is listed and the table usable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `measure of disability`
DECIDE `the measure under 1ב` `the injury is listed and the table usable` IS
    `the national-insurance regulations`

`1ב and 2ד measure a listed injury differently` MEANS
    (NOT (`the measure under 1ב` TRUE EQUALS `the measure under 2ד` TRUE))
#ASSERT `1ב and 2ד measure a listed injury differently`

-- 2א ¶2 and 2ב: "the insured sum" is the one in the insurance confirmation;
-- read with 1ב's 30,000 dollars for death and full disability, that is it.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_a akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_a/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_b
GIVEN a IS A `trip accident`, `insured sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `lump sum` a `insured sum` IS
    IF (NOT `the cover applies` a) THEN 0
    ELSE IF a's `died of it within 12 months`
         THEN `insured sum`
         ELSE (`insured sum` TIMES min (a's `disability percent`) 100) DIVIDED BY 100

-- 2ה: compensation for an accident never passes 100% of the insured sum.
-- F-1.10-j: whether the weekly and monthly sums of 1ג–ד (and the
-- committee's increase) count toward that cap is not said. The reading
-- adopted: the cap is on the lump sum of the table, 2א–ד, alone.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_2__subpara_e
GIVEN a IS A `trip accident`, `insured sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `capped lump sum` a `insured sum` IS
    min (`lump sum` a `insured sum`) `insured sum`

@export The compensation in dollars (paid in shekels) a teaching employee hurt on a school trip is owed under section 1.10.1 of the takanon, before any offset
GIVEN a IS A `trip accident` @desc the accident and its outcome
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `trip-accident compensation` a IS
    IF a's `insured by another insurer`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `capped lump sum` a `the sum for death or full disability, in dollars`
         PLUS `weekly compensation in dollars` a
         PLUS `monthly expenses in dollars` a

-- 3: the exclusions (with 1ז, carried in `the cover applies`).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_3/p1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_3__subpara_a akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_3__subpara_b akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_3__subpara_c akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_3__subpara_d
DECLARE `cause of injury` IS ONE OF
    `self-inflicted harm, suicide or an attempt`
    `needless deliberate danger`
    `an offence other than a traffic offence`
    `insanity, drunkenness or drugs`
    `a traffic offence`
    `another cause`

GIVEN c IS A `cause of injury`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `excluded by 3` c IF
    (NOT (c EQUALS `a traffic offence` OR c EQUALS `another cause`))

-- 4: the insured's duties. Time in days from the accident.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_4__subpara_a
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.10 party` `cover action`
DECIDE `the insured cooperates` IS
    PARTY `the insured or his representative`
    MUST  `cooperate with the insurer`
    WITHIN 365

-- 4ב: notice in writing as soon as possible, on death at once; the insurer
-- is not liable without notice within 6 months (about 182 days).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_4__subpara_b akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_4__subpara_b/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_4__subpara_b/p3
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.10 party` `cover action`
DECIDE `notice of the accident` IS
    PARTY `the insured or his representative`
    MUST  `notify the insurer in writing`
    WITHIN 182
    HENCE (PARTY `the insured or his representative`
           MUST  `send the accident report and doctor's certificate`
           WITHIN 10
           LEST BREACH BY `the insured or his representative` BECAUSE "section 1.10.1.4ג: the report and certificate follow within 10 days of the notice")
    LEST BREACH BY `the insured or his representative` BECAUSE "section 1.10.1.4ב: without written notice within 6 months the insurer is not liable"

-- 4ג: medical care at once; the report within 10 days of the notice
-- (above); the insurer may ask for more and for an examination; no claim
-- without a qualified doctor's confirmation.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_4__subpara_c akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_4__subpara_c/p2
GIVEN `confirmed by a qualified doctor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurer may recognise the claim` `confirmed by a qualified doctor` IF
    `confirmed by a qualified doctor`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_4__subpara_d
GIVEN `the insured has disappeared` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `presumed dead by accident` `the insured has disappeared` IF
    FALSE

-- 5: what the cover pays is set off against anything the government or
-- employer owes for the same event; nothing is owed where another insurer
-- covers it (carried in `trip-accident compensation`).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_5/p1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1__para_5/p2
GIVEN `owed by the government or employer for the event` IS A NUMBER, `paid under the cover` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `still owed by the government or employer` `owed by the government or employer for the event` `paid under the cover` IS
    max 0 (`owed by the government or employer for the event` MINUS `paid under the cover`)

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1/p1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1/p4 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1/p5 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_10__ssec_1_10_1/p6 The subsection's sources (אסמכתא): director-general's circulars.

-- Worked examples. Every salary figure is a placeholder.
`a day trip home at 19:30` MEANS
    `outing` WITH `starts in the morning` IS TRUE, `start hour` IS 8, `end hour` IS 19.5, `nights` IS 0, `end hour of the last day` IS 19.5

#ASSERT `activity units` `a day trip home at 19:30` EQUALS 3.5
#ASSERT `outing pay` `a day trip home at 19:30` 10000 0.5 0 FALSE EQUALS 122.5
#ASSERT `activity units` (`outing` WITH `starts in the morning` IS TRUE, `start hour` IS 8, `end hour` IS 17, `nights` IS 2, `end hour of the last day` IS 17) EQUALS 16

